{
    "$comment": "Which browser tests a change needs [scope-33]. Every test carries @component:<name>, @theme:<name> or @sweep (gates/check-tags.mjs refuses one that does not). A changed file is matched against `rules` in order, first match wins; `selectors` turns the rules a stylesheet change touches into components. gates/tags.mjs reads this file; `npm run test:tags` runs what it selects. The measurement against the old selection is under `measured`.",
    "levels": {
        "building": "the tags of the changed files only, firefox",
        "commit": "building plus every @sweep test, firefox",
        "release": "every test, chromium and firefox (npm run test:browser), on Kenny's go"
    },
    "measured": {
        "date": "2026-09-14",
        "how": "The last 20 commits on round-six that touched css/, js/, components/ or catalogue/ (5e95786 … 6ee15bf), each replayed with `node gates/run-tags.mjs --commit <sha> --dry-run` against the old gates/affected.mjs, counted with `playwright test --list --project=firefox` against the tests of 95dd39b (1251 per engine).",
        "old": "affected.mjs said `all` for all 20: every commit touched a stylesheet, a module or a catalogue file, so it ran 1251 tests each time, 25020 in total",
        "building": "9156 in total; 5 of 20 commits still select everything (js/strings.js in four, package.json in one); a catalogue-shell commit selects 47, a formal register commit 157, one catalogue page 63-171",
        "commit": "13599 in total (building plus the 352 @sweep tests)",
        "skipped": "Every test the old selection ran and the building level does not is a test the map holds uncoupled from the change: catalogue-shell commits skip every test that never opens a catalogue page; a register commit skips the other themes' slices of the sweeps (the commit level runs them) and the tests of components its rules do not name; a catalogue page skips the fixture-page tests of its component. What the map cannot see: a module that fails to load breaks every page that bundles it, and a keyframe name declared in several registers is decided by load order. Both reach far beyond their tags; the commit level's @sweep catches the first on every sweep page, and only the release level catches everything.",
        "commitDuration": "Sample 2026-09-14, firefox, 4 workers: tests/registers.spec.mjs (95 @sweep) 32.7 s, tests/fixtures.spec.mjs (132 @sweep) 31.4 s — 227 sweeps in 64 s, so the 352 @sweep tests run in about 100 s and a commit level in about two to three minutes"
    },
    "components": {
        "button": "buttons and icon buttons: catalogue/button.html, .kp-button",
        "switch": "the switch: catalogue/switch.html, .kp-switch",
        "field": "fields, forms and the drawn select: catalogue/field.html, .kp-field, js/forms.js",
        "combobox": "combobox and tag input: catalogue/combobox.html, .kp-combobox, .kp-tag",
        "datepicker": "the date picker: catalogue/datepicker.html, .kp-datepicker",
        "upload": "upload: catalogue/upload.html, .kp-upload",
        "colorpicker": "the colour picker: catalogue/colorpicker.html, .kp-colorpicker",
        "table": "the plain table and its scroll region: catalogue/table.html, .kp-table, js/tables.js",
        "datatable": "the data table: catalogue/table.html, .kp-datatable, js/datatable.js",
        "feedback": "alerts, toasts, badges, progress: catalogue/feedback.html",
        "overlays": "dialogs, popovers, menus, tooltips, confirmations: catalogue/overlays.html",
        "navigation": "nav bar, side navigation, tabs, breadcrumb, back to top: catalogue/navigation.html",
        "structure": "accordion, tree, timeline, split, reorder, wizard: catalogue/structure.html",
        "data": "showing data and the small patterns: catalogue/data.html",
        "media": "media, grid layout, marquee: catalogue/media.html",
        "page": "skip link, footer, command palette, theme menu: catalogue/page.html",
        "page-effects": "the effects module and what registers do with it: catalogue/page-effects.html, js/effects.js, fx/",
        "catalogue": "the catalogue shell, judging and verdicts: catalogue/*.js, catalogue/verdicts.json",
        "picker": "theme selection: the picker, theme-core, the registry, no-flash, lazy registers, diagnostics",
        "layout": "the layout layer: css/layout.css",
        "utilities": "the utility API: css/utilities.css",
        "fonts": "the shipped faces: fonts/, css/fonts.css",
        "examples": "the example and concept pages: examples/, showcase/examples.mjs, showcase/concept-*",
        "showcase": "the showcase and its per-theme pages: showcase/",
        "site": "the documentation site: site/, gates/site/",
        "bundle": "the dist bundle and the minified build: dist/"
    },
    "rules": [
        { "path": "docs/**", "none": "documentation; no browser reads it" },
        { "path": "*.md", "none": "documentation; no browser reads it" },
        { "path": ".claude/**", "none": "agent and hook configuration" },
        { "path": ".github/**", "none": "release and pages workflows" },
        { "path": ".githooks/**", "none": "the commit hook" },
        { "path": "reports/**", "none": "generated reports" },
        { "path": "ha/**", "none": "Home Assistant themes; no browser test loads them" },
        { "path": "**/*.d.ts", "none": "type declarations; npm run gates checks them" },
        { "path": "LICENSE", "none": "licence text" },
        { "path": ".gitignore", "none": "repository housekeeping" },
        { "path": ".gitattributes", "none": "repository housekeeping" },
        { "path": ".prettierignore", "none": "formatting configuration" },
        { "path": ".prettierrc", "none": "formatting configuration" },
        { "path": ".nvmrc", "none": "node version pin; a different node is a different run anyway" },
        { "path": "jsconfig.json", "none": "type checking only" },
        { "path": "tsconfig.types.json", "none": "type generation only" },
        { "path": "themes/{theme}/anatomy.md", "tags": ["@theme:{theme}"], "why": "the theme's own notes, beside its register" },
        { "path": "gates/site/**", "tags": ["@component:site"] },
        { "path": "gates/colour.mjs", "referenced": true, "why": "imported by specs; the specs that import it run" },
        { "path": "gates/config.json", "referenced": true },
        { "path": "gates/**", "none": "node gates; npm run gates runs them, and a generator's output is committed and mapped on its own" },
        { "path": "package.json", "all": "scripts and dependencies reach every test" },
        { "path": "package-lock.json", "all": "a dependency, Playwright included, reaches every test" },
        { "path": "playwright.config.mjs", "all": "the runner's configuration reaches every test" },
        { "path": "tests/global-setup.mjs", "all": "builds every React fixture" },
        { "path": "tests/fixtures/server.mjs", "all": "serves every page" },
        { "path": "tests/tags.json", "all": "the map itself; the whole selection may move" },
        { "path": "tests/*.spec.mjs", "spec": true, "why": "the changed spec file runs whole" },
        { "path": "tests/**", "referenced": true, "why": "a helper, fixture or data file: the specs that name it run" },

        {
            "path": "css/formal-register.css",
            "tags": ["@theme:formal"],
            "css": "selectors",
            "fallback": ["@sweep"],
            "why": "formal is the default theme: most fixtures and every catalogue page wear it, so a changed rule reaches every test of its component, not only that component's sweeps"
        },
        {
            "path": "css/{theme}-register.css",
            "tags": ["@theme:{theme}"],
            "css": "sweeps",
            "why": "the theme's own tests and its slice of every sweep, plus the sweeps of the components whose rules changed"
        },
        { "path": "themes/{theme}/**", "tags": ["@theme:{theme}"] },
        { "path": "themes/**", "tags": ["@sweep", "@component:picker"], "why": "order.json, hooks.json, known-asymmetry.json: every theme at once" },
        { "path": "css/themes.css", "css": "selectors", "fallback": ["@sweep"], "why": "generated token blocks per theme; a block names its theme" },
        { "path": "css/_rules.css", "css": "selectors", "fallback": ["@sweep"] },
        { "path": "css/_header.css", "tags": ["@sweep"] },
        { "path": "css/_density.css", "tags": ["@sweep", "@component:button", "@component:field"] },
        { "path": "css/_print.css", "tags": ["@sweep"] },
        {
            "path": "css/components.css",
            "css": "selectors",
            "fallback": ["@sweep", "*file"],
            "why": "a changed rule maps to the component its selector names; a rule naming none maps to @sweep and every component in the file"
        },
        { "path": "css/layout.css", "tags": ["@component:layout"] },
        { "path": "css/utilities.css", "tags": ["@component:utilities"] },
        { "path": "css/tailwind-bridge.css", "none": "no browser test loads it" },
        { "path": "css/fonts.css", "tags": ["@component:fonts"] },
        { "path": "fonts/**", "tags": ["@component:fonts"] },

        { "path": "js/datatable.js", "tags": ["@component:datatable"] },
        { "path": "js/tables.js", "tags": ["@component:table", "@component:datatable"] },
        { "path": "js/datepicker.js", "tags": ["@component:datepicker", "@component:datatable"] },
        { "path": "js/locale.js", "tags": ["@component:datepicker", "@component:datatable", "@component:upload"] },
        { "path": "js/combobox.js", "tags": ["@component:combobox", "@component:field", "@component:datatable"] },
